# Process 3, the body of portal.New: boxes 3.1 to 3.3 in the order it calls
# them, and box 3.4, the portal handler's answer to each request that box 9
# sends it. New does not call box 3.4: a handler's answer is drawn in the
# diagram of the function that builds the handler, after the entity that
# calls it, as box 9.4 is in flow.9.dfd. The router travels to box 9 as the
# portal handler and comes back as the receiver of box 3.4, whose fixed
# fields, like the reloader's source and builder, need no store.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number --number-prefix 3. docs/flow.3.dfd -o flow.3.svg

{6 Add the chat}
> portal configuration
[3.1. Check the portals and their sections and open the content directory of each docs section
 so that every input and toc path stays inside the documentation root
 (portal.openPortals)]
    > content directory path
    < content directory handle
    <Documentation root>
>
[3.2. Load the Elements assets
 or refuse to start without them
 (portal.loadAssets)]
> portal configuration, sites, Elements assets
[3.3. Build the router, whose routes send each request to a portal's page by the portal's slug: a spec section's viewer page or raw spec, or a docs section's document list, document page or raw file, with the document sidebar from the section's toc file when it names one; the home page, the Elements assets, the 404 page of a preview folder at /previews/, and with a chat its routes, each portal's chat page behind the check of the other routes of its portal
 so that box 3.4 answers each request with the router's sites, hooks and routes
 (portal.newRouter)]
> portal handler
{9 Wrap the portal handler in the reloader}
> response writer, request
[3.4. Answer each request with the pages of the portals and sections visible to its reader
 (portal.router.ServeHTTP)]

# type: portal configuration = portal.Config
# type: sites = []*portal.site
# type: content directory handle = io/fs.FS
# type: Elements assets = io/fs.FS
# type: portal handler = net/http.Handler
# type: response writer = net/http.ResponseWriter
# type: request = *net/http.Request
